From ff9d147ee33dcb6c688a3e8b7c0a8c93ef98b8f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Executor <codex-executor@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 13:16:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/23] sheet route: one carrier layout builder, symmetric
 carrier by default

Every entry point of the sheet route (production command, prototype driver,
surface census, block validation, rotation check) built its own carrier
layout, so the label definition could drift between them.  They now call
sheet_label_pipeline.build_carrier_layout, which applies the route's
carrier triangulation (CARRIER_TRIANGULATION, now the cube-symmetric
parity diagonal of commit 534c56b) in one place.  The rotation check keeps
--carrier-triangulation to compare against the frozen fan, the production
receipt records which rule produced the label, and SheetSolidContract
carries the rule as a frozen constant of the route.
